; Everything after "--" on the command line is a query term, never an
; option.  The scan that applies --now ahead of the other options must
; stop there too: "--now=foo" below is a query term that matches no
; account, not a --now option with a bad date.

i 2018/12/15 10:00:00 Work:ProjectA
o 2018/12/15 12:00:00

i 2018/12/15 13:00:00 Work:ProjectB
o 2018/12/15 15:00:00

test reg -- ProjectB or --now=foo
18-Dec-15                       Work:ProjectB                 2.00h        2.00h
end test
